 "notes": "Red 'This Work' curve (combined initial + higher-frequency data, coefficient-separation method) from the top panel (|d_e|) of Fig. 3, extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure Limitsproj.pdf. Axes calibrated from the figure's decade gridlines (x: 1e-20 to 1e-13 eV, y: 1e-8 to 1e6); the curve's x-extent matches the abstract's stated mass band 4.4e-19 to 6.8e-14 eV exactly. Curve downsampled to ~86 points by per-bin median in log-mass (narrow noise spikes smoothed). Paper assumes local DM density 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (matches canonical, no rescaling); 95% CL. Damour-Donoghue convention alpha(phi)=alpha(1+d_e*phi) with rho_DM = m^2 phi_0^2/(2*kappa^2), identical to the canonical d_e definition, so no conversion applied. The paper also bounds |d_me - d_g| (bottom panel); d_e chosen as the standard compilation plane. Caveat: the abstract quotes best limit d_e >~ 1.59e-1, but the plotted Fig. 3 curve's minimum is ~1.4 at ~3e-18 eV (factor ~9 higher); calibration was cross-checked against gridlines and the rendered figure, so the reported points follow the published curve rather than the abstract number. The green 'Future Exp' projection curve was excluded.",
